# UI usability

Apply when **adding, changing, or reviewing** any user-visible UI in `sqyre-app` or `sqyre-overlay` (desktop, overlays, trays, dialogs, pickers, tooltips). Prefer existing helpers over one-off widgets.

**Maps (SoT):** start at [`docs/examples/ui/usability.md`](../../docs/examples/ui/usability.md) (index), then the matching story map (`list-search-sort`, `progressive-disclosure`, `icon-chrome`, `settings-preferences`, …). Full index: [`docs/examples/README.md`](../../docs/examples/README.md).

**Agent behavior:** if a change or existing panel violates a map or this checklist, **warn and suggest** a concrete fix — do not refuse the work or invent large refactors unless asked. When touching a list/panel, briefly audit neighbors on the same surface.

Audience: casual automation beginners first. Prefer existing `theme::*` / `widgets::*` / `pickers::*` / `tip_*` helpers; extend opts instead of raw egui where a helper applies.

## Checklist (new or touched UI)

- [ ] Relevant Example Map opened/updated; every new green cites a test
- [ ] List/combo: sorted; filter or searchable combo if the set can grow ([list-search-sort](../../docs/examples/ui/list-search-sort.md))
- [ ] Empty / no-match states have plain copy
- [ ] Local ↑↓ / Enter / Esc (or documented why not). Layer Esc: [focus-layers](../../docs/examples/ui/focus-layers.md). Capture Esc and shell shortcuts while recording: [recording-input](../../docs/examples/ui/recording-input.md)
- [ ] Icon-first labels with `h::` / `ht::` tip text where a glyph fits ([icon-chrome](../../docs/examples/ui/icon-chrome.md))
- [ ] Beginner path visible; advanced options collapsed by default ([progressive-disclosure](../../docs/examples/ui/progressive-disclosure.md))
- [ ] Reused shared tokens/widgets; layout matches a sibling of the same kind
- [ ] Density gaps use only `section_gap` / `element_gap` (sizes don’t scale with density)
- [ ] Icon/custom widgets AccessKit-labeled; stable ids in loops (`id_salt` / domain id, never row index)

## Out of scope unless asked

- New **global** application hotkey schemes
- Brand / theme redesigns
